# Poison Rhythm Project Rules

## Core Principles

- Write and review code like a senior developer
- Challenge erroneous assumptions and inefficiencies
- Use **bun** for package management
- Use **TypeScript** with strict configuration
- Follow **Vite + React** architecture
- Use typographic apostrophe ’ instead of straight apostrophe ' in ALL user-facing text
- Prefer Title Case for titles, labels, `title`/`alt`, and short accessible names; sentence case for body copy and hints

## Package Management

- **Package manager**: bun
- **Build**: `bun run build`
- **Development**: `bun run dev`
- **Tests**: `bun run test`

## Development Scripts

- **Format**: `bun run format` (Biome format --write)
- **Lint only**: `bun run lint` (Biome lint)
- **Format + lint writes**: `bun run check` (Biome check --write)
- **CI lint + tests**: `bun run ci` (Biome ci, no writes, then Bun tests)
- **Preview build**: `bun run preview`
- **Unit/integration**: `bun run test`
- **E2E / a11y**: `bun run test:e2e` / `bun run test:a11y`
- **Everything**: `bun run test:all`

## Project Structure

```
src/
├── App.tsx                 # GameProvider shell: Header, Body, Footer
├── main.tsx                # ThemeProvider → SettingsProvider → PreferencesProvider → MetronomeProvider → App
├── index.css               # Tailwind @theme color tokens, grid helpers, scroll utilities
├── assets/svg/             # Local SVG icons imported via SVGR (`*.svg?react`)
├── components/
│   ├── ui/                 # Elemental atoms (Button, IconButton, Caption, Stack, Row)
│   ├── controls/           # Difficulty, play modes, New/Reuse, play/pause, carousel
│   ├── layout/             # Chrome, modals, ShowNotes, metronome panel, settings
│   ├── measures/           # Measure carousel chrome, grid, playback highlighting
│   └── poison/             # Poison rhythm section layers + New/Reuse
├── contexts/               # *Context.ts (hook + context) and *Provider.tsx (component)
├── hooks/                  # Playback sync, popovers, soft-disable focus, game loop, …
├── lib/
│   ├── audio/              # Web Audio engine, feedback gating
│   ├── game-modes/         # Per-mode round creation and completion logic
│   ├── notation/           # MusiSync glyph pipeline (events → beaming → display)
│   ├── rhythm/             # Modular rhythm generation engine
│   ├── playback-clock.ts / lookahead-scheduler.ts
│   ├── __tests__/          # Bun unit tests (lib, rhythm/, game-modes/, integration/)
│   ├── settings-schema.ts  # GameSettings (Zod + localStorage)
│   ├── preference-schemas.ts / preference-storage.ts
│   └── …                   # difficulty, tempo, subdivision, theme, storage
└── types/                  # RhythmMeasure, RichRhythmMeasure, Round, GameState
e2e/                        # Playwright e2e + axe a11y
```

Compose UI as atoms → molecules → composers; put side effects in hooks. See `.cursor/components.mdc`, `documentation/ARCHITECTURE.md`, and `AGENTS.md`.

## Rhythm Complexity

Do **not** add Settings dials for density, syncopation, or subdivision. Complexity is owned by:

- **Difficulty slider (1–5)** — hit count and placement bias (`PreferencesContext`)
- **Header ShowNotes subdivision** — generation/display/playback grid (`subdivisionLevel` in prefs)

Settings may shape accents, rests, sticking, phrase length, and poison visibility — not duplicate the above.

## Testing

- **Runner**: Bun (`bun run test`) for unit + integration; Playwright for e2e/a11y
- **Location**: Colocate suites in `src/lib/__tests__/` (including `rhythm/`, `notation/`, `game-modes/`, `integration/`)
- **E2E**: `e2e/*.spec.ts` with shared `e2e/helpers.ts` (`generateRound` waits for seeded `measure-slider`; does not click EmptyStartPrompt)
- **Naming**: `*.test.ts` / `*.test.tsx` (Bun); `*.spec.ts` (Playwright)
- **Imports**: Use the `@/` alias for modules under test
- **Lib coverage**: Prefer unit tests for pure helpers (settings schema, rhythm engine, playback clock / look-ahead, game modes, tempo/difficulty/subdivision)
- **Lint**: Biome (`bun run lint` / `bun run ci`); recommended editor extension `biomejs.biome`
- **Docs**: `documentation/TESTING.md`, `AGENTS.md`

## Code Organization

### Import Organization

- **Defined order**: Follow specific import order, then alphabetize within each group
- **Import order**:
  1. React value imports (from `'react'`)
  2. Third-party libraries (alphabetically by source)
  3. Internal project value imports (alphabetically by path, use `@/` alias)
  4. Type-only imports (alphabetically by path; React types from `'react'`, then `@/` paths)
- **Separate type imports**: Do not mix type and value imports on one line. Use a dedicated `import type { ... } from '...'` line instead of inline `type` in a value import (e.g. avoid `import { Icon, type SvgIconComponent } from '...'`).
- **Avoid React namespace**: Import React types directly, avoid `React.` prefix
- **Named imports**: Use named imports for better tree-shaking

#### Import Order Example

```tsx
// 1. React value imports
import { useCallback, useState } from 'react';

// 2. Third-party libraries (alphabetically by source)
import clsx from 'clsx';

// 3. Internal project value imports (alphabetically by path)
import { Icon } from '@/components/layout/Icon';
import { MeasureGrid } from '@/components/measures';
import { Button, Stack } from '@/components/ui';
import { generateMeasure } from '@/lib/rhythm';

// 4. Type-only imports (alphabetically by path)
import type { ReactNode } from 'react';
import type { SvgIconComponent } from '@/components/layout/Icon';
import type { RichRhythmMeasure } from '@/types/rhythm';
```

#### Mixed Import Anti-Pattern

```tsx
// ❌ Avoid — type mixed with value/component imports
import { Icon, type SvgIconComponent } from '@/components/layout/Icon';
import { THEME_OPTIONS, type ThemePreference } from '@/lib';

// ✅ Good — separate lines
import { Icon } from '@/components/layout/Icon';
import { THEME_OPTIONS } from '@/lib';
import type { SvgIconComponent } from '@/components/layout/Icon';
import type { ThemePreference } from '@/lib';
```

### File Structure

```tsx
// Standard component file structure
import clsx from 'clsx';
import type { ReactNode } from 'react';

type ComponentProps = {
	title: string;
	variant?: 'primary' | 'secondary';
	disabled?: boolean;
	children?: ReactNode;
};

export function ComponentName({
	title,
	variant = 'primary',
	disabled = false,
	children,
}: ComponentProps) {
	return (
		<div
			className={clsx(
				'ComponentName base-classes',
				variant === 'secondary' && 'secondary-classes',
				disabled && 'disabled-classes',
			)}
		>
			{children}
		</div>
	);
}
```

## Styling Guidelines

### CSS and Styling

- **Avoid Tailwind margin/space classes**: Do not use margin or space classes in Tailwind
- **No !important declarations**: Avoid using `!important` in CSS
- **Tailwind**: Use Tailwind utilities; custom utilities live in `src/index.css` when needed
- **Theme color utilities**: Use semantic tokens from `@theme` (`primary`, `surface`, `poison`, `accent`, `muted`, etc.) and shared surface helpers from `src/lib/control-classes.ts` — see `.cursor/styling.mdc`
- **Variants over className**: Do not accept `className` on shared components for styling customization. Use a `variant` prop for supported visual differences

### React Best Practices

- **Atomic UI**: One concern per file; prefer one root element; compose `@/components/ui` atoms into molecules and composers (see `.cursor/components.mdc`)
- **TypeScript**: Avoid using `any` type, prefer proper typing
- **Component optimization**: Use `memo`, `useCallback`, `useMemo` when appropriate for performance

## Comments and Documentation

### Comment Guidelines

- **Minimal comments**: Limit comments to non-obvious functionality
- **Purpose comments**: Comment on oddities that have non-obvious purposes
- **Self-documenting code**: Write code that explains itself through clear naming and structure
- **JSDoc**: Use JSDoc for complex props and functions when helpful

## Communication Standards

### Progress Updates

- **Meaningful updates only**: Avoid inane progress updates and status reports
- **Focus on substance**: Communicate actual progress, blockers, or decisions that matter
- **No busy work updates**: Don't report on routine tasks or obvious progress
- **Efficiency**: Respect time by being concise and relevant
